PATCH 228: reconstruct FUN_0000_502f (object-render setup) -- a DGROUP-near-offset base-loss + a Ghidra
shared-ret control-flow misread.  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x502f-0x5078.

Reached as the mission render prep enumerates the roster objects (di=0xc05c enemy slot).  502f guards the
object then publishes it into the 0x7ae0 render fields + far-calls the seg-0xf69 service 0x703d
(FUN_1000_66cd) with a per-object service-id, and marks 0x87bd/0x87d6.  Ghidra base-lost di (host-deref ->
SIGSEGV) and merged the guard-fail ret so it wrongly wrote on that path; reconstructed faithfully with the
early returns, the explicit g_mem+0x1c000 base, and the asm byte/word widths.

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows.  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.  Sources
pristine; fist.c via build/.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -14155,24 +14155,31 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_502f(int *param_1)
 
 {
-  undefined2 uVar1;
