+     &0x20) -- Ghidra restructured the shared ret so it wrongly zeroed 0x7ae0 AND wrote 0x87bd/0x87d6 on the
+     guard-FAIL path; the asm writes NOTHING on guard-fail.  On pass: publish the object into 0x7ae0, copy
+     byte[di+0x1b]->0x7ae2, set 0x7ae7=0xfa, pick a service-id si (0xc84, or byte[di+0x43]-indexed table
+     0x86bc if word[di+0x40]&1), far-call 0f69:0x703d=FUN_1000_66cd(si), then set 0x87bd/0x87d6=3.  Ghidra
+     base-lost di (host-deref -> SIGSEGV at 0xc05c) and mis-scaled the word accesses.  Rebased through
+     g_mem+0x1c000 with the asm byte/word widths. */
+  unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+  unsigned int di = (unsigned short)(uintptr_t)param_1;
+  if (di == 0) return;                                                 /* or ax,ax; je 5078 */
